# Purpose
# Use one wrapper command for build, smoke, or serve workflows.
#
# Common usage
# Run from the repository root.
# .\scripts\pages-local.ps1 -Mode Build
# .\scripts\pages-local.ps1 -Mode Smoke -Port 4000
# .\scripts\pages-local.ps1 -Mode Serve -Port 4000
# .\scripts\pages-local.ps1 -Mode Serve -Port 4001 -SkipBuild
#
# Useful options
# -Mode chooses Build, Smoke, or Serve.
# -Port chooses the localhost port.
# -BindAddress chooses the local bind address.
# -SkipBuild serves or smokes the current _site folder.
# -SkipSetup skips dependency setup before build.
# -NoClean keeps the current _site folder before build.
# -Environment sets JEKYLL_ENV for the build.
#
# Recommended next command
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -SkipBuild -Port 4000
#
# Notes
# This is the preferred entry point for everyday local use.
# Serve mode keeps the webserver running.
